{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity","excerpts":[["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:absorb","absorption and descent","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.html#eq:recurrences\">(1)</a>. If <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> for every <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> implies <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. For any positive integer\nsequence <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>, eventual nonnegativity\nof <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> implies its eventual\nvanishing.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:barrier","Chinese remainder theorem and first\ncrossing","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>u</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> tend\nto infinity and let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> be an\ninteger with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi></math></span> for\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>. There is no sequence of\npairwise coprime integers <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span>\nfor which <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> whenever\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:bounded","bounded negative part","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, and </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟶</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>for all sufficiently large </mtext><mi>n</mi></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> for some integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>,\nthen <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> for all sufficiently\nlarge <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:cor","","<p><em> Under Theorem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.html#res:bounded\" data-universe-ref=\"statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:bounded\">4.1</a>, the multipliers\nsatisfy <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>\neventually.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:crt","consecutive multiples","<p><em> For pairwise\ncoprime integers <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></span> and every lower\nbound, there is a larger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>t</mi></math></span> such\nthat <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></math></span> for each <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>B</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:cubicrate","cubic-rate irrationality","<p><em> A\nstrictly increasing sequence of positive integers with </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> has\nirrational reciprocal sum.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:frontier","necessary profile","<p><em> The integer\ntail of a sequence satisfying Problem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.html#res:problem\">1.1</a>’s hypotheses but not\nits conclusion has <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>\neventually, <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>,\nunbounded negative magnitudes along negative indices, and </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:gcdstab","gcd stabilisation","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.html#eq:recurrences\">(1)</a>. If some fixed\ninteger <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> satisfies <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> at infinitely many\nindices, then <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is\neventually constant. Dividing <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> by its eventual value gives\ncoprime sequences satisfying the same recurrences.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:inclusiveone","an inclusive one-sided <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span> bound","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>⋯</mo></math></span> be positive integers\nwith <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></munder><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>. Suppose that for some\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mstyle displaystyle=\"false\"><mtext>for all large </mtext></mstyle><mi>n</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then the sequence is eventually\nSylvester. In particular, the conclusion holds under the pointwise\neventual bound <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:lcmbounded","a bound using the least common\nmultiple","<p><em> Assume the hypotheses of Problem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.html#res:problem\">1.1</a>. Write <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>lcm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nwith <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> then the\nsequence is eventually Sylvester.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:massscalar","a convergent sum of relative increases","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> be positive integers\nand <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> integers satisfying <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>n</mi></munder><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em>\nthen <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> eventually. Neither\ndenominator dynamics nor vanishing relative error is required.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:originalbounded","bounded increments of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span>","<p><em> Let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>⋯</mo></math></span> be positive\nintegers, <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, and\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℚ</mi></mrow></math></span>. Put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span>. If </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">lim sup</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> for all sufficiently\nlarge <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>n</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:reduced","persistent coprimality","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> be integer sequences\nwith <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> satisfying </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. The <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></span> are pairwise coprime, and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo movablelimits=\"true\">gcd</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> whenever <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:residue","factorial residue reduction","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi></math></span> be a nonnegative integer and let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></math></span> be integers with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>b</mi><mspace width=\"0.444em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>mod</mi><mspace width=\"0.333em\" linebreak=\"nobreak\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>!</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>. The first <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>h</mi></math></span> steps of the recursion <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>num</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>,\nstarting at index zero, are integral for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math></span> if and only if they are integral\nfor <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:step","two zero errors","<p><em> For integer\nsequences satisfying <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.html#eq:recurrences\">(1)</a>, if <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, then <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>. In particular, if\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow></math></span> also satisfy <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, eventual zero error implies the\neventual Sylvester recurrence.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:update","error identities","<p><em> For integer\nsequences satisfying <a class=\"math-ref\" data-equation-ref=\"true\" href=\"papers/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.html#eq:recurrences\">(1)</a>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:weightedrecord","a convergent weighted sum over new\nmaxima","<p><em> Assume the growth and rationality hypotheses of\nProblem <a class=\"math-ref\" href=\"papers/erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity.html#res:problem\">1.1</a>. Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> be finite\nand nonincreasing, with <span class=\"math inline\"><math><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span>. Then the sequence is eventually Sylvester if\nand only if, for some integer <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>B</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>ℛ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-243-reciprocal-tail-rigidity#res:weights","weights and linear density","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span> be positive integers, let <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, and put <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></math></span>, with the sum\nallowed a priori to be <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span>.\nThen <span class=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo movablelimits=\"true\">lim inf</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>\nif and only if there is a finite nonincreasing <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><munder><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></math></span>.</em></p>"]]}
